# Sway(fonn) — session config
#
# Loaded by the "Sway(fonn)" entry on the login screen, via
#   /opt/sway-next/bin/sway-profile-session fonn
#
# Everything shared with the other sway sessions lives in ../common — bindings,
# modes, colors, window rules, daemons. Edit that and every session picks it up.
# Edit THIS file only for what should be true in Sway(fonn) and nowhere else.
#
# What IS specific to fonn: four screens, one app each. WHICH app goes on which
# screen is not written here — it lives in
#   ~/.config/sway-layouts/fonn.layout   (-> dot_files/layouts/fonn.layout)
# so the layout can change without touching sway config or reloading sway.

include ../common

### Screens — 1 terminal · 2 zen · 3 slack · 4 obsidian
exec $HOME/.local/bin/sway-layout fonn

### VPN
# Idempotent: does nothing if the tunnel is already up in Seattle, and moves it
# if it is up somewhere else. It waits for DNS first — sway's exec fires before
# NetworkManager is necessarily usable, and a bare `nordvpn connect` loses that
# race at login and fails silently, leaving you unprotected.
#
# Not in fonn.layout because that file is about which app owns which screen, and
# this opens no window.
exec $HOME/.local/bin/vpn-connect United_States Seattle
